WEBVTT

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.850
<i>A vampire I'm acquainted with moved 
into my neighborhood recently.</i>

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.830
Bottled blood isn't that bad
once you get used to it.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.300
I'd prefer to suck it out 
of a young girl, though.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.290
Ellie, have you ever considered 
that it's rude to empty out

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.760
<b>Smooth O
Rich AB
Light A</b>

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.770
someone's fridge like this?

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.130
You're right.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.420
I need to stop being a burden to you.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:43.350
<b>Tasty B</b>

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.680
I mean, I don't mind, as long 
as it's not <i>all</i> the time...

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.130
All right, then I'm going to go out hunting!

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.610
Wait.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.070
Why?

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.630
You've been asleep for a hundred years.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.480
I'm worried that you might not 
be ready for the present.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.500
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.500
<b>Vampire Cooking</b>

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.100
It'll be fine.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.700
I won't overdo it.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.930
This is a peaceful city.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.910
If someone started biting people, 
it would be a huge deal.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.750
I'm just going to start ordering
enough blood for you online, too.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.460
You can buy it with that?

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.130
Yeah.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.880
But then all the fun of finding 
just the right girl is gone.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.960
Depending on my mood, I choose 
based on the color of their hair,

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.860
or the color of their skin, 
or their personality...

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.680
You can pick your favorites 
when shopping online, too.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.540
But those aren't cute.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.150
<b>Grumpy</b>

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.900
I'll just pick something for you, then.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.220
Do you have any preference for 
a certain blood type or flavor?

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.660
What's most important is the face!

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.610
Then how about this "Beauty's Blood"?

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.410
Beauty's Blood

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:13.130
<b>Beauty's Blood</b>

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:13.130
<b>We've taken special care to 
control the diet and sleep
 schedule of the most beautiful 
people for several months
 before using a specially 
developed extraction method
to maintain the highest quality. 
Then, we deliver each bottle
to you using state of the art
 temperature control!!</b>

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.560
That exists?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.120
You can buy pretty much anything online.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.950
There's no need to go out
 in the middle of the day.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:19.770
If you need anything, I can just 
order it together with my stuff.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:23.290
That reminds me. It's convenient 
to have a fridge to keep

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:26.100
the blood cool, and a 
microwave to heat it up in.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.020
Sophie...

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.730
You're being so nice. Thank you.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.060
Having you cause a scene 
in the neighborhood

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.920
or turn into ash is just that much worse.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.610
Oh, this "Innocent Idol"
flavor sounds really good!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.990
<b>Utterly Lacks Self-Awareness</b>

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:44.450
What?! The stuff you ordered 
yesterday is already here?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.340
That really <i>is</i> convenient.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.650
What a great age!

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.070
I'm happy for you!

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:53.590
Seeing how simple it is makes me 
want to shop more and more!

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:58.540
I'd like to buy a TV, and I'd like 
to try one of those mobile phones.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.720
Maybe I'll learn how to use a computer, too.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.060
I did make a mess of that before.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:07.360
Ellie-chan's becoming a 
true child of this age.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.720
<i>If she keeps going like this,
she might actually pull it off.</i>

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:11.930
What's wrong?

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.330
Is this enough to pay for it,
 or do I need more?

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.200
Maybe you should get a 
sense of how money works

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.770
before you move on to computers.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.800
Hinata's here.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.340
Heya!

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.820
So that's Sophie's friend?

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.320
Yeah, this is Ellie-chan.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.620
She's a vampire, just like Sophie-chan.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.330
I'm Natsuki Hinata. It's nice to meet you.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.010
Nice to meet you, too.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.290
This girl looks pretty tasty.
Seems like the healthy type.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.930
Stop looking at my friends like that.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.130
Thanks for having me.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.520
We're having a slumber party tonight.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.030
Want to join, Ellie-chan?

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:55.160
We'll stay up late watching 
movies and chatting.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.170
That sounds like fun.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.710
<i>I think she'll get along 
just fine with them.</i>

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.590
It's Ellie-chan, huh?

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:05.110
I love children!

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:06.820
There, there.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.130
You're so adorable.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.350
And so small, you could be our little sister!

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:12.990
Who are you calling a child?

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.490
I'm over 450 years old!

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:18.710
R-Really? I thought you were 
younger than Sophie.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.470
What was that?

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.630
You think you can say whatever you 
want just because you've got boobs?!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.910
So impertinent!

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.480
S-S-Stop it!

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.550
What did you do to get them this big?

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.920
I didn't get this big because I wanted to!

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:36.100
How do you like this?! 
And this! And this! And this!

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.110
<i>She made her cry.</i>

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.560
You didn't have to make her cry.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.300
Go apologize to Hinata.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.420
I'm not crying.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:44.310
Excuse me?! She was rude to me first!

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.210
But there was no reason to get that mad!

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:49.600
Only children get this mad 
about being called a child!

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.210
What did you say?!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:51.820
Now, now...

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.940
Hinata-chan, why don't you 
apologize to Ellie-chan?

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:58.480
She didn't mean to hurt you, 
so you can still make up.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:00.560
But...

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.250
I'm going home!

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.630
Hinata-chan!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.450
Hinata-chan...

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:12.510
Whatever.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:14.770
Hinata-chan...

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.640
She was looking forward to
 us all hanging out together.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.600
I don't care.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:22.240
Ellie, you're not a child, you know.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.750
I guess we have no choice.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:36.470
We shouldn't make a young girl 
walk around alone at this hour.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.640
We're going after her.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:38.580
Ellie-chan!

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.650
Hurry up or I'm leaving you behind.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:41.510
Sure!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.580
I don't see her anywhere.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.040
That's so strange.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.970
This is the way she would take to walk home.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:56.040
I was wondering, though,
 why did you get so upset?

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.620
I was pretty surprised.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.740
Back when I was human,

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:05.870
I was really looking forward 
to becoming a grown-up.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.930
My mother was very beautiful,

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.850
and I thought that one day,
 I'd be like that, too.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:16.400
But I never had the chance.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.070
Ellie-chan...

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:21.220
Having someone tall with actual 
breasts treat me like a child

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.280
just made me snap.

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:24.970
I see...

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.650
If only I could've been a 
human for four more years...

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:34.160
I bet I would've had a nice 
body and grown taller, too.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:41.280
Well, I think you're really cute and
 wonderful the way you are right now!

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.260
You look like a doll!

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.160
Y-You think so?

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:47.700
Thank you.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.100
You have very weird taste, though.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.490
Weird?!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.440
Hey, isn't that Hinata?

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.530
You're right! It's Hinata-chan!

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:04.690
<i>That girl said she's over 450 years old.</i>

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:07.790
<i>She's spent hundreds of 
years in the body of a child.</i>

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.640
<i>Maybe it's something that really bothers her.</i>

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:13.400
<i>I said something insensitive.</i>

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:17.220
<i>But she said things I'm 
sensitive about, too.</i>

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.880
Natsuki's built like a dude,
but she's got pretty big boobs.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:22.180
<b>She's sensitive about it because her classmates made fun of her in middle school</b>

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.080
They don't suit you.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.020
Shut up!

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.520
<i>I called her a child, but I 
guess I'm not any different.</i>

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.990
<i>I was too proud to apologize.</i>

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.790
Hinata-chan!

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.630
Watch out!

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:50.790
Huh?

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.250
Looks like I made it.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.250
You're not hurt, are you?

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:56.710
E-Ellie...

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:00.050
Thank goodness!

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:00.950
Wh-Why are you crying?

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:02.470
Hinata's fine.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:04.740
Th-Thank you.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:06.900
Why did you help me, though?

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.140
I said something awful to you.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:11.100
Because I'm an adult.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:14.470
I came to own up to what 
I did and apologize.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.350
I'm sorry for how I acted earlier.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.950
It wasn't very mature of me.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.290
Besides, having big boobs is a good thing.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.120
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.960
You might be short, but you're 
an excellent older sister.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.100
It was wrong of me to 
treat you like a child.

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.780
As long as you get it, that's enough.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:38.180
You'd better not call me small again, though.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.530
Sorry! Sorry!

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.670
Say it once and make it count!

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:42.860
So did they make up?

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:44.100
I wonder...

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:49.010
<i>After that, the four of 
us had a slumber party.</i>

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.140
<i>It looks like Ellie's integrated somehow,</i>

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.910
<i>so a peaceful life seems plausible.</i>

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:03.990
Water...

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.280
What's that sound?

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.760
Oh, it's you, Ellie.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.970
Getting a late-night snack?

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:24.680
No.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.140
It's a monster!

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.740
That's not a nice thing to say.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:31.660
Putting blood on your face 
is good for your skin.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:34.150
Is everything okay?

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:37.460
What happened?

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.720
Modern people are so skillful!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.580
They can even sleep standing up.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.730
<i>Looks like life's going to be 
even more rowdy than before.</i>

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:55.480
Sophie, that fridge thing that came 
to my house doesn't get cold at all.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.000
Did you plug it in?

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.360
What do you mean?

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.920
Thank you, Sophie!

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.670
I'll call you if I need anything else.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:07.290
Jeez...

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:10.520
She even made me help 
set up her other appliances.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:14.860
It takes quite a bit longer 
for it to get dark now.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:16.980
I guess it's already that time of year.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.460
Oh, isn't that Mori-san from next door?

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:25.540
Let me help you.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:28.960
Oh, Sophie-chan. Thank you!

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:31.950
I've gotten so exhausted 
that I just can't move.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.510
I see.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.170
You can't move?

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.270
Excuse me.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.510
Sophie-chan, you're much 
stronger than you look.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.130
This is normal for a vampire.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:48.240
My daughter is bringing my 
grandchild over tomorrow.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:52.880
That's why I was thinking I'd 
go shopping and surprise them

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:56.190
with a bunch of special delicious dishes!

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.460
Then I ended up buying way too much.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:02.040
So it makes humans happy 
when you make them food?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.400
That's right!

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:06.090
Tomorrow, I'm really going all-out.

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:08.690
There's going to be 
beef stroganoff, a gratin,

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:11.980
roast beef, paella, salt-grilled sea bream,

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:16.260
and ohagi and pie and
 tarts and bavarois and...

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:19.420
Can they actually eat all that?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:26.780
This braid looks so cute on you!

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:29.290
<i>I should cook something for Akari, too.</i>

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.400
<i>She's always helping me out.</i>

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.910
You're being so sweet today. I love it!

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.830
<i>She said she was going out 
tomorrow, so I can wake up early,</i>

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:41.260
<i>and while she's out...</i>

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.940
That was close. I almost went back to sleep.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.910
I'll be back soon!

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:55.710
Yes.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:02.400
<i>I bet she'll be so shocked when she 
comes home and sees all the food I made.</i>

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.190
What's wrong, Akari?

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:07.620
Did you forget something?

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:14.680
No, but you're actually up early today,
so maybe I should just cancel my trip.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.660
Today is the last day for this 
doll exhibit I wanted to see.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:21.970
But I don't want to be away from you!

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.630
Just go already.

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:26.360
And don't come back too early.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:29.260
You're so cold!

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:30.880
All right.

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:34.470
Thanks for coming over to help me, Hinata.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:36.220
It sounded like fun.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:37.460
I appreciate the help.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.230
Unfortunately, I'm not particularly 
good at cooking,

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.680
so I don't know how much help I'll be.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.430
I've only ever made curry and fried rice.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:49.590
I figured you could help me by 
telling me what kind of foods

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.380
Akari likes and doesn't like.

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:54.390
Well, sure! Ask me anything about Akari!

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:57.970
Her favorite foods, how she picks her 
utensils, her favorite clothing style,

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:00.310
what kind of underwear she wears, 
what kind of socks she likes...

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.350
Ask me anything!

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.390
That sounds promising.

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:06.030
You even know about her 
underwear and socks, huh?

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.740
W-Well, since we're both girls, 
it's normal to see each other

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.680
in underwear when we're changing for PE!

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.380
And socks are always in plain sight!

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:13.450
True.

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.320
<i>She averted her eyes!</i>

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:20.380
I bought a whole bunch 
of ingredients online.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.200
Wow, some of this stuff is pretty unusual.

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:26.400
I looked up a lot of things online.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:27.480
I worked hard on this.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:30.450
<i>A few of these things aren't even food!</i>

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:34.030
You know, dirt isn't edible.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:36.510
What on earth are you 
planning on feeding Akari?

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:37.060
<b>Shock</b>

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:41.100
A long time ago, I read in a book 
that soil is rich in minerals.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:43.890
That may be so, but at least 
around here, we don't eat it.

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.850
You even bought these?

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:49.730
I know that humans don't eat nails.

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:50.870
Everyone knows that.

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.070
Then why are they here with the ingredients?

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.070
The nails are for making stock!

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:58.830
By using the nails to make 
a soup rich in iron,

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.870
you can supply nutrients 
that many people tend to lack!

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:03.410
Uh, it's going to smell like iron.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.210
A soup that smells like iron...

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.290
That sounds good.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:10.520
Only to vampires.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.210
I see.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:14.440
Why don't we go shopping, then?

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:17.020
Could you pick out some of 
Akari's favorite foods?

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.060
I'm fine with doing that, but are you?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.520
It's still daytime.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.010
It's fine.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:25.390
For going to the local supermarket,
a parasol is all I need.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:33.940
You don't look so good.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.130
Don't force yourself.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:36.890
It's really sunny today.

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:39.740
I'm f-fine.

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:44.390
I just need to rest a bit in the 
shade and I'll recover, I think.

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.580
S-So this is it.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:54.180
Seriously? From one berry hitting you?

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.050
We made it home somehow.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:00.940
It must be hard for humans, 
having to shop for different

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:03.170
ingredients every day,
then having to prepare them.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.020
You think so?

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:07.660
Isn't it harder to not get sick 
of drinking blood every day?

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:10.790
I've got type A, type B, low fat...

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:12.160
High in platelets...

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.140
Darjeeling flavor...

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:14.270
Burgundy flavor...

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:15.310
Mocha flavor...

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:16.060
Cuvée...

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:16.930
American...

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.510
Traditional Chinese medicine blend....

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.260
I have so many flavors,
I never get sick of it.

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:23.310
<i>They all look the same, though.</i>

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.420
<b>Strawberry
Daifuku</b>

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.420
What's this?

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.110
Strawberry daifuku!

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:30.760
Those have been Akari's 
favorite since forever.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.180
Really?

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:35.620
That means if I put Akari's favorite, 
these strawberry daifuku,

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.810
into humans' favorite rice balls,

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:39.420
it'll create the ultimate delicacy!

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:40.190
Don't!

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:44.100
But combining bread with yakisoba 
and croquettes is considered good.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:49.100
Why are strawberry daifuku 
in rice balls no good?

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:56.020
I can't really explain it.
I just know it's wrong!

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:57.620
I see.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.410
Well, here's what I made.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.940
Sophie, this is not food.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.460
So it didn't turn out edible...

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.910
This is harder than I thought.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:15.300
What do you even want to make?

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.330
What's your plan?

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:20.610
I was thinking something healthy,
 something tasty,

00:17:20.610 --> 00:17:21.950
and something unusual.

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:24.670
Despite being so vague that 
you can't even picture it,

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:26.290
you sure have high aspirations.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:29.370
Making something unique is fine and all,

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.820
but it's safer for beginners to make 
things according to a recipe.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.320
<b>Tasty Recipes</b>

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:35.520
I see.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.960
It's really nice that they put in the 
exact ingredients and amounts.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.170
Salt...

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:41.430
A little?

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:42.430
As needed?

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:43.330
Skin?

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.800
Mushy?

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.640
How many grams is "as needed"?

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:49.240
What do they mean by "skin"?

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:52.650
What kind of state is this 
"mushy" of "boiling until mushy"?

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.510
Looks like it's another failure.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.610
Don't be too hard on yourself!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:04.980
The food we eat is different from yours,
and you don't get many opportunities to cook.

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:07.660
You did manage to make 
rice balls before, right?

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:09.280
Yes.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:12.730
Cooking rice in a rice cooker, 
shaping that into forms,

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:14.970
and arranging them on a plate 
is something I can do.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.580
Then why don't you try to 
put a spin on something

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.200
that you know you can do?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.670
Something I can do?

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:21.290
Yeah!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:26.750
<b>Japanese Rice</b>

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:30.330
<b>Western Rice</b>

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:30.330
<b>Rice Balls</b>

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:30.330
<b>Rice with Nori</b>

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:30.330
<b>Rice with Egg</b>

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:30.330
<b>Rice Porridge</b>

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:30.330
<b>A Table Full of White Rice</b>

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.030
I guess that might not work.

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:30.330
Yeah.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:38.610
I just wanted to make her 
something special so she'd be happy.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.820
I never imagined cooking was this hard.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:48.310
Just make something simple,
and don't try so hard. It'll turn out fine.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.480
But...

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.930
It'll be fine.

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:53.680
It doesn't have to be a fancy meal.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:57.930
Just knowing you were thinking of her 
will be enough to make her happy.

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:01.660
It's so delicious!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:02.990
Thank you, Sophie-chan!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.500
You're right.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:09.380
I could always teach you how to 
make any of the dishes I can make.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:10.960
Could I ask you to do that?

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.530
I'd like to have a soup and a dessert, too.

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:15.290
Your choices are either curry or fried rice.

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:18.660
All you have to do for curry is cut 
up the ingredients and stew them.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:24.900
It flew all the way over there?

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:29.010
A-Anyway, the carrots and potatoes are done,

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:30.380
so next is the onion.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:33.200
Why am I crying?

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.650
<i>I'm starting to wonder if 
she can actually do this...</i>

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:39.850
Okay, everything's in the pot, so now we just...

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:45.990
What if I add some strawberry 
daifuku as a secret ingredient?

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.490
<b>Strawberry
 Daifuku</b>

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.840
Don't try to think outside the box!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.580
<b>Strawberry
 Daifuku</b>

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:52.970
The last thing is this.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:58.650
It smells like garlic!

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:00.480
Hey, watch where you point that thing!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.930
<b>Garlic</b>

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:07.040
I guess the ingredients do list garlic.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:10.860
But if we don't put this in,
 it won't be curry.

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:14.470
Wait one second.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:17.690
Put it on low...

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:20.150
Now I'm fine.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.620
Let's continue.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:30.570
<i>That's not what you wear to make curry!</i>

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.540
All right. We added the roux.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.490
Is it curry now?

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:36.630
Not yet.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.500
We only just put it in.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:40.540
What about now?

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:41.640
Not yet.

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:42.400
Now?

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.240
No, not yet.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.430
Why is it taking so long?

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:48.030
I thought we used the roux 
so it would be done quickly.

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:49.720
Can't you wait ten minutes?!

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.180
<b>Minutes</b>

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.180
<b>Seconds</b>

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.180
<b>Start
Stop</b>

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:52.180
Okay, it's done!

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:54.160
Now, put it on the rice.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:56.490
Now it'll finally be...

00:20:58.510 --> 00:20:59.320
There!

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.890
It's done!

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:07.330
It looks so... normal, though.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:09.470
Just be glad it looks normal.

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:10.830
Stop complaining.

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:13.010
I'm home!

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:15.740
Oh, something smells good!

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:17.180
Welcome back.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:20.410
Akari, I tried to cook something.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:24.910
Oh, wow, this is amazing!

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:28.130
Sophie-chan really made this for me?

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.770
I'm so happy!

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:33.690
I'll treasure this to the end of my days!

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.190
Just eat it before it gets cold!

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:39.110
H-How is it?

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.270
Delicious!

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:45.170
R-Really?

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.410
If it's inedible, you don't 
have to force yourself.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:51.270
It's not at all! It really is delicious!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.760
Really?

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:55.300
I'm glad to hear it.

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.670
Why are you so far away?

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.260
Are you blushing?

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:00.990
Actually, that's the...

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:05.680
Hey, Sophie, that microwave 
thing is sparking and... uh...

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:10.030
It smells like garlic!

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:21.000
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:21.000
<b>Interview with the Vampire</b>
